IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- coa21-ch4-directors-report.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 28, Chapter 4 -- Amendments to Part 7 of the Companies Act 1985 (s 992).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Reading a result: see the header of coa21-ch1-panel.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING).
-- WHAT THIS IS. Section 992 amends another Act (the 1985 Act). The brief calls amendments of other Acts machinery (inert, reason 2), and
-- subsections (1) and (3) are left inert on that ground. But the text inserted by subsection (2) (paragraph 13 of Schedule 7 to the 1985 Act)
-- and by subsections (4) and (5) is itself an operative duty on directors and companies, so it is encoded as the provision states it
-- (a scope decision, recorded in NOTES.md under Marginal readings). The text does not say whether the inserted words are still in force: subsection (6) limits them to directors'
-- reports for financial years beginning on or after 20 May 2006, and that date is a plain input. Seams: s 1166 (employees' share scheme, the
-- keel) and s 1173(1) (regulated market, the keel).

§ `Part 28, Chapter 4: Amendments to Part 7 of the Companies Act 1985`

-- s 992(6): the amendments apply to directors' reports for financial years beginning on or after 20 May 2006.
-- src:13924 | (6) The amendments made by this section apply in relation to directors' reports for financial years beginning on or after 20th May 2006.
@ref s 992(6) Matters to be dealt with in directors' report (src:13924-13924)
GIVEN `the first day of the financial year` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 992(6) the amendments apply to the directors' report` MEANS
    IF `the first day of the financial year` AT LEAST (Date 20 5 2006)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the amendments "apply in relation to directors' reports for financial years beginning on or after 20th May 2006", and the text is silent about earlier years

-- Schedule 7 paragraph 13(1) (inserted by s 992(2)): Part 7 applies to the directors' report for a year if the company had securities carrying voting rights admitted to trading on a regulated market at the end of it.
-- src:13874 | (1) This Part of this Schedule applies to the directors' report for a financial year if the company had securities carrying voting rights admitted to trading on a regulated market at the end of that year.
@ref s 992(2) para 13(1) Matters to be dealt with in directors' report (src:13874-13874)
GIVEN `s 1173(1) the company had securities carrying voting rights admitted to trading on a regulated market at the end of the financial year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 992(2) para 13(1) this Part of Schedule 7 applies to the directors' report` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1173(1) the company had securities carrying voting rights admitted to trading on a regulated market at the end of the financial year`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part of this Schedule applies to the directors' report for a financial year if the company had securities carrying voting rights admitted to trading on a regulated market at the end of that year."
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "regulated market" is Article 2.1.13 of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014 (section 1173(1))

-- Schedule 7 paragraph 13(4) (inserted): a person has an indirect holding of securities if they are held on his behalf or he can secure that the rights are exercised in accordance with his wishes.
-- src:13905 | (4) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (2)(c) a person has an indirect holding of securities if—
-- src:13906 | (a) they are held on his behalf, or
-- src:13907 | (b) he is able to secure that rights carried by the securities are exercised in accordance with his wishes.
@ref s 992(2) para 13(4) Matters to be dealt with in directors' report (src:13905-13907)
GIVEN `the securities are held on the person's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is able to secure that rights carried by the securities are exercised in accordance with his wishes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 992(2) para 13(4) the person has an indirect holding of securities` MEANS
    IF `the securities are held on the person's behalf` OR `the person is able to secure that rights carried by the securities are exercised in accordance with his wishes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person has an indirect holding of securities if— (a) they are held on his behalf, or (b) he is able to secure that rights carried by the securities are exercised in accordance with his wishes"

-- Schedule 7 paragraph 13(3) (inserted): a company's capital includes any securities not admitted to trading on a regulated market.
-- src:13904 | (3) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (2)(a) a company's capital includes any securities in the company that are not admitted to trading on a regulated market.
@ref s 992(2) para 13(3) Matters to be dealt with in directors' report (src:13904-13904)
GIVEN `the securities are not admitted to trading on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 992(2) para 13(3) the securities are part of the company's capital for sub-paragraph (2)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the securities are not admitted to trading on a regulated market`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a company's capital includes any securities in the company that are not admitted to trading on a regulated market"

-- Schedule 7 paragraph 13(2) (inserted): the matters on which the report must contain detailed information, and the limits in (2)(c), (d), (e) and (5).
DECLARE `s 992(2) para 13(2) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 992(2) para 13(2)(a) the structure of the company's capital`
    `s 992(2) para 13(2)(b) any restrictions on the transfer of securities in the company`
    `s 992(2) para 13(2)(c) each person with a significant direct or indirect holding of securities in the company`
    `s 992(2) para 13(2)(d) each person who holds securities carrying special rights with regard to control of the company`
    `s 992(2) para 13(2)(e) how the control rights of an employees' share scheme are exercisable`
    `s 992(2) para 13(2)(f) any restrictions on voting rights`
    `s 992(2) para 13(2)(g) any agreements between holders of securities that may result in restrictions on the transfer of securities or on voting rights`
    `s 992(2) para 13(2)(h) any rules about the appointment and replacement of directors or the amendment of the articles`
    `s 992(2) para 13(2)(i) the powers of the company's directors`
    `s 992(2) para 13(2)(j) any significant agreements that take effect, alter or terminate upon a change of control following a takeover bid`
    `s 992(2) para 13(2)(k) any agreements providing for compensation for loss of office or employment because of a takeover bid`

-- src:13875 | (2) The report shall contain detailed information, by reference to the end of that year, on the following matters—
-- src:13876 | (a) the structure of the company's capital, including in particular—
-- src:13877 | (i) the rights and obligations attaching to the shares or, as the case may be, to each class of shares in the company, and
-- src:13878 | (ii) where there are two or more such classes, the percentage of the total share capital represented by each class;
-- src:13879 | (b) any restrictions on the transfer of securities in the company, including in particular—
-- src:13880 | (i) limitations on the holding of securities, and
-- src:13881 | (ii) requirements to obtain the approval of the company, or of other holders of securities in the company, for a transfer of securities;
-- src:13882 | (c) in the case of each person with a significant direct or indirect holding of securities in the company, such details as are known to the company of—
-- src:13883 | (i) the identity of the person,
-- src:13884 | (ii) the size of the holding, and
-- src:13885 | (iii) the nature of the holding;
-- src:13886 | (d) in the case of each person who holds securities carrying special rights with regard to control of the company—
-- src:13887 | (i) the identity of the person, and
-- src:13888 | (ii) the nature of the rights;
-- src:13889 | (e) where—
-- src:13890 | (i) the company has an employees' share scheme, and
-- src:13891 | (ii) shares to which the scheme relates have rights with regard to control of the company that are not exercisable directly by the employees,
-- src:13892 | how those rights are exercisable;
-- src:13893 | (f) any restrictions on voting rights, including in particular—
-- src:13894 | (i) limitations on voting rights of holders of a given percentage or number of votes,
-- src:13895 | (ii) deadlines for exercising voting rights, and
-- src:13896 | (iii) arrangements by which, with the company's co-operation, financial rights carried by securities are held by a person other than the holder of the securities;
-- src:13897 | (g) any agreements between holders of securities that are known to the company and may result in restrictions on the transfer of securities or on voting rights;
-- src:13898 | (h) any rules that the company has about—
-- src:13899 | (i) appointment and replacement of directors, or
-- src:13900 | (ii) amendment of the company's articles of association;
-- src:13901 | (i) the powers of the company's directors, including in particular any powers in relation to the issuing or buying back by the company of its shares;
-- src:13902 | (j) any significant agreements to which the company is a party that take effect, alter or terminate upon a change of control of the company following a takeover bid, and the effects of any such agreements;
-- src:13903 | (k) any agreements between the company and its directors or employees providing for compensation for loss of office or employment (whether through resignation, purported redundancy or otherwise) that occurs because of a takeover bid.
-- src:13904 | (3) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (2)(a) a company's capital includes any securities in the company that are not admitted to trading on a regulated market.
-- src:13905 | (4) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (2)(c) a person has an indirect holding of securities if—
-- src:13906 | (a) they are held on his behalf, or
-- src:13907 | (b) he is able to secure that rights carried by the securities are exercised in accordance with his wishes.
-- src:13908 | (5) Sub-paragraph (2)(j) does not apply to an agreement if—
-- src:13909 | (a) disclosure of the agreement would be seriously prejudicial to the company, and
-- src:13910 | (b) the company is not under any other obligation to disclose it.
@ref s 992(2) para 13(2) and (5) The matters the directors' report must cover (src:13875-13910)
GIVEN `s 992(2) para 13(1) this Part of Schedule 7 applies to the directors' report` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 992(2) para 13(2) matter`
      `the person has a significant direct or indirect holding of securities in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds securities carrying special rights with regard to control of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1166 the company has an employees' share scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `shares to which the scheme relates have rights with regard to control of the company that are not exercisable directly by the employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `disclosure of the agreement would be seriously prejudicial to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is not under any other obligation to disclose the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 992(2) para 13(2) the report must contain detailed information on the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 992(2) para 13(1) this Part of Schedule 7 applies to the directors' report`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part of this Schedule applies to the directors' report for a financial year if the company had securities carrying voting rights admitted to trading on a regulated market at the end of that year."
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the Part applies depends on "regulated market" (section 1173(1))
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER matter
        WHEN `s 992(2) para 13(2)(a) the structure of the company's capital` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 992(2) para 13(2)(b) any restrictions on the transfer of securities in the company` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 992(2) para 13(2)(c) each person with a significant direct or indirect holding of securities in the company` THEN
            IF `the person has a significant direct or indirect holding of securities in the company` THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "significant" is not defined, and the paragraph is "in the case of each person with a significant direct or indirect holding"
        WHEN `s 992(2) para 13(2)(d) each person who holds securities carrying special rights with regard to control of the company` THEN
            IF `the person holds securities carrying special rights with regard to control of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph is "in the case of each person who holds securities carrying special rights with regard to control of the company"
        WHEN `s 992(2) para 13(2)(e) how the control rights of an employees' share scheme are exercisable` THEN
            IF `s 1166 the company has an employees' share scheme` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `shares to which the scheme relates have rights with regard to control of the company that are not exercisable directly by the employees`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where— (i) the company has an employees' share scheme, and (ii) shares to which the scheme relates have rights with regard to control of the company that are not exercisable directly by the employees"
        WHEN `s 992(2) para 13(2)(f) any restrictions on voting rights` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 992(2) para 13(2)(g) any agreements between holders of securities that may result in restrictions on the transfer of securities or on voting rights` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 992(2) para 13(2)(h) any rules about the appointment and replacement of directors or the amendment of the articles` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 992(2) para 13(2)(i) the powers of the company's directors` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 992(2) para 13(2)(j) any significant agreements that take effect, alter or terminate upon a change of control following a takeover bid` THEN
            IF `disclosure of the agreement would be seriously prejudicial to the company` AND `the company is not under any other obligation to disclose the agreement`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Sub-paragraph (2)(j) does not apply to an agreement if— (a) disclosure of the agreement would be seriously prejudicial to the company, and (b) the company is not under any other obligation to disclose it."
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 992(2) para 13(2)(k) any agreements providing for compensation for loss of office or employment because of a takeover bid` THEN JUST TRUE

-- Schedule 7 paragraph 13(6) (inserted): the definitions.
-- src:13912 | “securities” means shares or debentures;
@ref s 992(2) para 13(6)“securities” Matters to be dealt with in directors' report (src:13912-13912)
GIVEN `the thing is a share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a debenture` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 992(2) para 13(6) the thing is securities` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a share` OR `the thing is a debenture`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“securities” means shares or debentures"

-- src:13913 | “takeover bid” has the same meaning as in the Takeovers Directive;
@ref s 992(2) para 13(6)“takeover bid” Matters to be dealt with in directors' report (src:13913-13913)
GIVEN `the offer is a takeover bid within the meaning of the Takeovers Directive` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 992(2) para 13(6) the offer is a takeover bid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offer is a takeover bid within the meaning of the Takeovers Directive`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“takeover bid” has the same meaning as in the Takeovers Directive"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Takeovers Directive is not among the sources

-- src:13914 | “the Takeovers Directive” means Directive 2004/25/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council;
@ref s 992(2) para 13(6)“the Takeovers Directive” Matters to be dealt with in directors' report (src:13914-13914)
GIVEN `the instrument is Directive 2004/25/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 992(2) para 13(6) the instrument is the Takeovers Directive` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is Directive 2004/25/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the Takeovers Directive” means Directive 2004/25/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council"

-- src:13915 | “voting rights” means rights to vote at general meetings of the company in question, including rights that arise only in certain circumstances..
@ref s 992(2) para 13(6)“voting rights” Matters to be dealt with in directors' report (src:13915-13915)
GIVEN `the rights are rights to vote at general meetings of the company in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 992(2) para 13(6) the rights are voting rights` MEANS
    IF `the rights are rights to vote at general meetings of the company in question`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- including rights that arise only in certain circumstances
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“voting rights” means rights to vote at general meetings of the company in question"

-- s 992(4): a directors' report must also contain any necessary explanatory material about the information Part 7 of Schedule 7 requires (new section 234ZZA(5)).
-- src:13917 | (4) After that subsection insert—
-- src:13918 | (5) A directors' report shall also contain any necessary explanatory material with regard to information that is required to be included in the report by Part 7 of Schedule 7..
@ref s 992(4) Matters to be dealt with in directors' report (src:13917-13918)
GIVEN `Part 7 of Schedule 7 requires information to be included in the directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report contains the necessary explanatory material about that information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 992(4) the directors' report contains the explanatory material section 234ZZA(5) requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Part 7 of Schedule 7 requires information to be included in the directors' report`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "information that is required to be included in the report by Part 7 of Schedule 7"
    ELSE IF `the report contains the necessary explanatory material about that information`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A directors' report shall also contain any necessary explanatory material with regard to information that is required to be included in the report by Part 7 of Schedule 7."

-- s 992(5): a company that sends a summary financial statement instead of the directors' report must include the explanatory material in the statement or send it at the same time (new section 251(2ZB)).
-- src:13919 | (5) In section 251 (summary financial statements), after subsection (2ZA) insert—
-- src:13920 | (2ZB) A company that sends to an entitled person a summary financial statement instead of a copy of its directors' report shall—
-- src:13921 | (a) include in the statement the explanatory material required to be included in the directors' report by section 234ZZA(5), or
-- src:13922 | (b) send that material to the entitled person at the same time as it sends the statement.
-- src:13923 | For the purposes of paragraph (b), subsections (2A) to (2E) apply in relation to the material referred to in that paragraph as they apply in relation to a summary financial statement..
@ref s 992(5) Matters to be dealt with in directors' report (src:13919-13923)
GIVEN `the company sends an entitled person a summary financial statement instead of a copy of its directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement includes the explanatory material required to be included in the directors' report by section 234ZZA(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company sends that material to the entitled person at the same time as it sends the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 992(5) the company has complied with section 251(2ZB)` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company sends an entitled person a summary financial statement instead of a copy of its directors' report`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "A company that sends to an entitled person a summary financial statement instead of a copy of its directors' report"
    ELSE IF `the statement includes the explanatory material required to be included in the directors' report by section 234ZZA(5)` OR `the company sends that material to the entitled person at the same time as it sends the statement`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall— (a) include in the statement the explanatory material required to be included in the directors' report by section 234ZZA(5), or (b) send that material to the entitled person at the same time as it sends the statement"

-- src:13919 | (5) In section 251 (summary financial statements), after subsection (2ZA) insert—
-- src:13920 | (2ZB) A company that sends to an entitled person a summary financial statement instead of a copy of its directors' report shall—
-- src:13921 | (a) include in the statement the explanatory material required to be included in the directors' report by section 234ZZA(5), or
-- src:13922 | (b) send that material to the entitled person at the same time as it sends the statement.
-- src:13923 | For the purposes of paragraph (b), subsections (2A) to (2E) apply in relation to the material referred to in that paragraph as they apply in relation to a summary financial statement..
@ref s 992(5) Matters to be dealt with in directors' report (src:13919-13923)
GIVEN `the material is sent under paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 992(5) subsections (2A) to (2E) of section 251 apply to the material` MEANS
    IF `the material is sent under paragraph (b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of paragraph (b), subsections (2A) to (2E) apply in relation to the material referred to in that paragraph as they apply in relation to a summary financial statement."
